00:14:22,661 --> 00:14:24,400
both priced around $60,000.

172
00:14:25,500 --> 00:14:27,860
Breaking Point will return on Modern Marbles.

173
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:33,840
We like to think of the world surrounding us as stable and solid.

174
00:14:35,560 --> 00:14:39,420
But everything in it is poised to shatter when it reaches its breaking point.

175
00:14:43,260 --> 00:14:47,740
Underwriters Laboratories has studied electrical and fire safety since 1894,

176
00:14:48,740 --> 00:14:51,280
when a series of fires at the Chicago World's Fair

177
00:14:51,281 --> 00:14:53,300
prompted an investigation.

178
00:14:55,580 --> 00:14:59,520
The company built its reputation by establishing safety standards.

179
00:15:00,680 --> 00:15:02,820
It's twisted wires to the breaking point,

180
00:15:03,940 --> 00:15:05,780
tested light switches and bulbs,

181
00:15:06,700 --> 00:15:08,560
and set fire to roofing materials.

182
00:15:10,300 --> 00:15:12,960
Now it tests everything from household appliances

183
00:15:12,961 --> 00:15:15,620
to various kinds of bulletproof glass.

184
00:15:16,400 --> 00:15:19,020
Often bullet-resistant materials are layered.

185
00:15:19,021 --> 00:15:23,140
you might have glass up front, but behind it you might have a plastic material.

186
00:15:23,280 --> 00:15:27,240
So if a bullet does impinge on the glass and particles do come off the glass,

187
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:29,520
it's caught by the plastic material in back,

188
00:15:29,640 --> 00:15:32,600
thus protecting the person behind the bulletproof glass.

189
00:15:33,680 --> 00:15:36,360
With our camera in position, we're ready to go.

190
00:15:38,660 --> 00:15:42,160
